Validate an EBPPS header and stop reserving k up front.

Found by data.sketches tools/fuzz:

- The sample reserved all of k (from the image, up to 2^31 - 2) at
  construction, so a 20-byte image claiming a large k allocated gigabytes
  (out-of-memory). The reservation is a hint; it is now capped and the
  vector grows. This also spares ebpps(k = 1e9) in R the same allocation.
- A non-empty image must have n > 0, a positive finite cumulative and
  maximum weight and rho in (0, 1]; otherwise it re-serializes as a
  different sketch (n == 0 reads back as empty).

--- a/sampling/include/ebpps_sample_impl.hpp	2026-11-16 21:33:12
+++ b/sampling/include/ebpps_sample_impl.hpp	2026-11-16 21:33:12
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include "ebpps_sample.hpp"
 #include "serde.hpp"
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <limits>
 #include <string>
@@ -40,7 +41,10 @@
   partial_item_(),
   data_(allocator)
   {
-    data_.reserve(reserved_size);
+    // The reservation is only a hint; reserving all of k up front made an
+    // empty sketch with a large k (or a 20-byte image claiming one) allocate
+    // gigabytes. The vector grows as items arrive.
+    data_.reserve(std::min<uint32_t>(reserved_size, 1u << 12));
   }
 
